    >[x] Take no nesting from inside parse errors in Core =core-error-structure $Core's tolerant parse builds actions out of tree-sitter error recovery, so a skipped level (\[ ] Root then >>\[ ] Skipped) can load under Root when recovery shifts, as the conflict-marker prototype showed. Keep no parent link that comes from inside an ERROR node and report E004/E005 from Core. Done when test_unsupported_grammar_rules asserts the result directly (not only if Ok) and passes on the current and the prototype grammar.$ !1 ^2026-11-25T23:53 %2026-11-26T00:44 #01a21521-541a-75b2-8ecf-4ab1ee196ee0
